# `vercel --prod` uploads the WORKING TREE, and `next build` type-checks everything it
# finds. That means any scratch script a session leaves lying around becomes a build
# input — and one written with a hardcoded local path ("/Users/…/data/points-tabs.json")
# fails the deploy with an error about a file that exists perfectly well on the laptop.
# It cost a production deploy on 14 Aug. Nothing below is imported by the app, so none of
# it belongs in a build.
#
# NOTE: adding this file makes Vercel stop consulting .gitignore for uploads, so anything
# that must not ship needs to be listed HERE too. node_modules and .git are always excluded.
scripts
db
docs
*.tsbuildinfo
.next
.vercel
